IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the injured seafarer meets:
-- whether the Act covers my employment (ss 4, 19, 20, 20A), whether what I suffered is an "injury" (ss 3, 9), whether
-- compensation is payable (s 26), notice and the claim (ss 62, 63), when my employer is taken to have refused it (ss 72,
-- 73, 73A), travel to treatment (s 28(6), (7)), my weekly compensation after the first 45 weeks and when it stops (ss 31,
-- 38), permanent impairment (ss 39, 40(4)), compensation on death (s 29), and reconsideration and review (ss 78, 88).
--
-- SEAT: the employee (a seafarer or trainee). "I was injured as a seafarer on a ship the Act covers. Am I covered, and
-- what compensation do I get?" Unlike the Comcare scheme, the EMPLOYER is liable and determines the claim (ss 24, 25);
-- it asks its own questions in sea-seat-employer.l4, which calls the rules here and restates none of them.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 34, compilation date 21 February 2025, includes amendments up to Act No. 14, 2025 (register id
-- C2025C00116), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04525.txt.
--
-- FORMULAS LOST IN THE DEPOSIT. Section 31(2) (the first 45 weeks), s 13 (normal weekly earnings), s 28(6A)(b), s 41(2)
-- and s 23A(3) read "the formula: where:" with nothing between. Section 31(5), for every later week, is in words, and is
-- computed here; the first 45 weeks are answered as a band, not an amount. See NOTES.md finding 1.
--
-- INDEXED AMOUNTS ARE INPUTS: the s 31(9)-(11) minimum earnings figures, the s 39(9) maximum (CPI, s 23) and the s 29
-- death amounts (WPI, s 23A), each with the compilation's printed figure in its @desc; AWOTE (s 31(7)) likewise.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Employment the Act does not reach answers `not covered`. Sections 5, 7, 10 (presumed diseases), 11, 13,
-- 27, 30, 31(2) amount, 32 to 37, 40(1)-(3), 41 to 47, Part 3 (rehabilitation), Part 4 (common law), ss 64 to 71, 74,
-- 75, 80 to 86, Parts 6 onwards (insurance beyond s 93, the Fund, the Authority).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992 -- the injured seafarer's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `employment the Seafarers Act does not reach is under another workers compensation law, which is not encoded (ss 19, 20, 20A)`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `ss 4, 19, 20, 20A -- does the Act cover my employment`

-- s 4(1): "employee means: (a) a seafarer; or (b) a trainee; or (c)" a person registering at a Seafarers Engagement
-- Centre. s 3: "seafarer means a seafarer, as defined in the Navigation Act 2012, who is employed in any capacity on a
-- prescribed ship, on the business of the ship"; a prescribed ship is one Part II of the Navigation Act 1912 would have
-- applied to, or declared, but not a Government ship (asked as a fact).
-- s 19(1): the Act "applies to the employment of employees on a prescribed ship that is engaged in trade or commerce: (a)
-- between Australia and places outside Australia; or (aa) between 2 places outside Australia; or (b) among the States; or
-- (c) within a Territory, between a State and a Territory or between 2 Territories" (not a ship on the Australian
-- International Shipping Register, the note to (1)); (1AA) a vessel in coastal trading under a general licence (or an
-- emergency licence, if on the Australian General Shipping Register); (2) to (4) also to the employees of a trading,
-- financial or foreign corporation. s 20: it "does not apply to a person who is an employee within the meaning of the
-- Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988". s 20A: the Authority may exempt employment on a ship.
DECLARE `My role` IS ONE OF
    `a seafarer employed on a prescribed ship, on the ship's business`
    `a company or industry trainee`
    `a seafarer between ships, required to register at a Seafarers Engagement Centre`
    `something else`

DECLARE `The ship's trade` IS ONE OF
    `overseas, or between two places outside Australia`
    `interstate, or within or between Territories`
    `coastal trading under a general licence, or an emergency licence on the Australian General Shipping Register`
    `within one State only`

GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role`
      `the ship's trade` IS A `The ship's trade`
      `my employer is a trading, financial or foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is on the Australian International Shipping Register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a Comcare employee under the SRC Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my employment is exempt under s 20A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act covers my employment` IF
        (NOT (`my role` EQUALS `something else`))
    AND (NOT `the ship is on the Australian International Shipping Register`)
    AND (NOT `I am a Comcare employee under the SRC Act`)
    AND (NOT `my employment is exempt under s 20A`)
    AND (    (NOT (`the ship's trade` EQUALS `within one State only`))
         OR  `my employer is a trading, financial or foreign corporation`)

@export Does the Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act cover my employment (ss 4, 19, 20, 20A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `My role` @desc What you are: a seafarer employed on a prescribed ship (not a Government ship), a trainee, a seafarer registering availability at a Seafarers Engagement Centre, or something else
      `the ship's trade` IS A `The ship's trade` @desc The trade or commerce the ship is engaged in
      `my employer is a trading, financial or foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer is a trading or financial corporation formed in Australia, or a foreign corporation (most shipping companies are)
      `the ship is on the Australian International Shipping Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ship is registered in the Australian International Shipping Register
      `I am a Comcare employee under the SRC Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988 (employed by the Commonwealth, a Commonwealth authority or a Comcare licensee)
      `my employment is exempt under s 20A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Seafarers Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Authority has exempted your employment on the ship
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Does the Act cover my employment` MEANS
    IF `the Act covers my employment` `my role` `the ship's trade` `my employer is a trading, financial or foreign corporation` `the ship is on the Australian International Shipping Register` `I am a Comcare employee under the SRC Act` `my employment is exempt under s 20A`
    THEN `answered` TRUE
    ELSE `not covered` `employment the Seafarers Act does not reach is under another workers compensation law, which is not encoded (ss 19, 20, 20A)`

§§ `ss 3, 9 -- is it an injury`

-- s 3: "injury means: (a) a disease; or (b) an injury (other than a disease) ..., being a physical or mental injury
-- arising out of, or in the course of, the employee's employment; or (c) an aggravation ... but does not include
-- anything suffered by an employee as a result of reasonable disciplinary action taken against the employee, or failure
-- by the employee to obtain a promotion, transfer or benefit in connection with his or her employment." "disease means
-- ... an ailment or an aggravation that was contributed to in a material degree by the employee's employment."
-- s 9(2): an injury is treated as so arising if it happened "(a) as a result of an act of violence that would not have
-- occurred apart from the employment"; "(b) if the employee is a seafarer: (i) while the employee was on board the
-- prescribed ship ...; or (ii) while ... temporarily absent from that ship during an ordinary recess ... and not at his or
-- her place of residence"; "(e) while the employee: (i) was travelling between his or her place of residence and place
-- of work", and other listed journeys and places. (3): not a journey "by a route that substantially increased the risk"
-- or "interrupted in a way that substantially increased the risk". (4): not at a place or in a recess where the employee
-- "voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk of injury".
DECLARE `What I suffered` IS ONE OF
    `an ailment or disease, or its aggravation`
    `a physical or mental injury, other than a disease, or an aggravation of one`

DECLARE `Where I was hurt` IS ONE OF
    `on board the ship I was employed on`
    `ashore on an ordinary break from the ship, not at home`
    `travelling between home and work, or another journey listed in s 9(2)(e)`
    `at training, at a Seafarers Engagement Centre, or at a place for a medical certificate, treatment or payment`
    `by an act of violence that would not have happened apart from my job`
    `somewhere else`

GIVEN `where I was hurt` IS A `Where I was hurt`
      `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my route or a break in the journey substantially increased the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9 treats it as arising out of or in the course of employment` IF
    CONSIDER `where I was hurt`
    WHEN `somewhere else` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `by an act of violence that would not have happened apart from my job` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `travelling between home and work, or another journey listed in s 9(2)(e)` THEN (NOT `my route or a break in the journey substantially increased the risk`)
    OTHERWISE (NOT `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk`)

DECLARE `Is it an injury` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is an "injury" under s 3`
    `no: a disease must have been contributed to in a material degree by my employment (s 3)`
    `no: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, my employment (ss 3, 9)`
    `no: it resulted from reasonable disciplinary action, or a failure to get a promotion, transfer or benefit (s 3)`

@export Is what happened to me an "injury" under the Seafarers Act (ss 3, 9)?
GIVEN `what I suffered` IS A `What I suffered` @desc Whether it is a disease or ailment (or its aggravation), or a physical or mental injury other than a disease (or its aggravation)
      `my work contributed to it in a material degree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a disease: whether your employment contributed to it in a material degree (your employer's judgment, on review the Tribunal's)
      `where I was hurt` IS A `Where I was hurt` @desc For an injury other than a disease: where or how it happened
      `it otherwise arose out of or in the course of my work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For an injury other than a disease: whether it arose out of, or in the course of, your employment in some other way
      `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on board, at a listed place or on a break, you were hurt because you voluntarily and unreasonably exposed yourself to an abnormal risk
      `my route or a break in the journey substantially increased the risk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a journey: whether you took a route, or interrupted the journey, in a way that substantially increased the risk of injury compared with a more direct route
      `it resulted from reasonable discipline or a missed promotion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it resulted from reasonable disciplinary action taken against you, or from failing to get a promotion, transfer or benefit
GIVETH AN `Is it an injury`
`Is it an injury under the Seafarers Act` MEANS
    IF `it resulted from reasonable discipline or a missed promotion`
    THEN `no: it resulted from reasonable disciplinary action, or a failure to get a promotion, transfer or benefit (s 3)`
    ELSE IF `what I suffered` EQUALS `an ailment or disease, or its aggravation`
         THEN IF `my work contributed to it in a material degree`
              THEN `yes: it is an "injury" under s 3`
              ELSE `no: a disease must have been contributed to in a material degree by my employment (s 3)`
         ELSE IF     `s 9 treats it as arising out of or in the course of employment` `where I was hurt` `I voluntarily and unreasonably submitted to an abnormal risk` `my route or a break in the journey substantially increased the risk`
                 OR  `it otherwise arose out of or in the course of my work`
              THEN `yes: it is an "injury" under s 3`
              ELSE `no: it did not arise out of, or in the course of, my employment (ss 3, 9)`

§§ `s 26 -- is compensation payable`

-- s 26(1): "If an employee suffers an injury that results in his or her death, incapacity for work, or impairment,
-- compensation is payable for the injury." (2): not "for an intentionally self-inflicted injury". (3): not for one "caused
-- by the serious and wilful misconduct of the employee, unless the injury results in death, or serious and permanent
-- impairment." s 28(2): medical expenses whether or not the injury results in death, incapacity or impairment.
DECLARE `Is compensation payable` IS ONE OF
    `yes: compensation is payable for the injury (s 26(1)), and for reasonable medical treatment (s 28)`
    `only medical expenses: the injury has not resulted in death, incapacity for work or impairment (ss 26(1), 28(2))`
    `no: an intentionally self-inflicted injury is not compensated (s 26(2))`
    `no: an injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct is not compensated unless it results in death or serious and permanent impairment (s 26(3))`

@export Is compensation payable to me for my injury (ss 26, 28(2))?
GIVEN `it has caused incapacity for work, impairment or death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury has resulted in incapacity for work, an impairment, or death
      `it was intentionally self-inflicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was intentionally self-inflicted
      `it was caused by my serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by your own serious and wilful misconduct
      `it caused death or serious and permanent impairment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury resulted in death or in a serious and permanent impairment
GIVETH AN `Is compensation payable`
`Is compensation payable to me` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it was intentionally self-inflicted` THEN `no: an intentionally self-inflicted injury is not compensated (s 26(2))`
        IF `it was caused by my serious and wilful misconduct` AND (NOT `it caused death or serious and permanent impairment`)
            THEN `no: an injury caused by my serious and wilful misconduct is not compensated unless it results in death or serious and permanent impairment (s 26(3))`
        IF `it has caused incapacity for work, impairment or death` THEN `yes: compensation is payable for the injury (s 26(1)), and for reasonable medical treatment (s 28)`
        OTHERWISE `only medical expenses: the injury has not resulted in death, incapacity for work or impairment (ss 26(1), 28(2))`

§§ `ss 62, 63 -- notice and the claim`

-- s 62(1): the Act "does not apply to an injury ... unless a written notice of the injury is given to the employer ... as
-- soon as practicable after the employee becomes aware of the injury". (3): "if the injury was suffered by an employee on
-- a prescribed ship, a notice given to the master of the ship is taken to be given to the employer." (4): a defective
-- notice counts if the employer is not prejudiced, or for death, absence from Australia, ignorance, mistake or another
-- reasonable cause. s 63(2): a written claim in the approved form, "(b) except where the claim is for compensation under
-- section 28, 29 or 30--a certificate by a legally qualified medical practitioner", and "(c) a notice setting out" any
-- other employer claimed against or whose employment is believed to have contributed. (3): without the certificate, the
-- claim is taken not to be made until it is given. (4): substantial compliance is enough.
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `medical expenses, compensation on a death, or funeral costs (ss 28 to 30)`
    `weekly incapacity, permanent impairment or another kind of compensation`

@export Have I given notice and made a claim that counts (ss 62, 63)?
GIVEN `I gave written notice to my employer or the ship's master as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave written notice of the injury to your employer (or, for an injury on the ship, to its master) as soon as practicable after becoming aware of it
      `a late or defective notice is excused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: whether the employer would not be prejudiced, or the failure came from absence from Australia, ignorance, a mistake or another reasonable cause
      `I made a written claim substantially in the approved form, naming any other employer involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave your employer a written claim substantially in the approved form, with the notice naming any other employer you have claimed against or whose employment you believe contributed
      `the kind of claim` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc What the claim is for
      `I gave a medical practitioner's certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave a certificate from a medical practitioner on the approved form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I made a claim that counts under the Seafarers Act` IF
        (`I gave written notice to my employer or the ship's master as soon as practicable` OR `a late or defective notice is excused`)
    AND `I made a written claim substantially in the approved form, naming any other employer involved`
    AND (`I gave a medical practitioner's certificate` OR `the kind of claim` EQUALS `medical expenses, compensation on a death, or funeral costs (ss 28 to 30)`)

§§ `ss 72, 73, 73A -- when is my claim taken to be refused`

-- s 73(2): for a claim about incapacity for work, property, or the cost of medical treatment, the employer "must determine
-- its liability ... by the latest of the following times: (a) the end of the period of 12 days after the day on which the
-- employer receives the claim; (b) if the employer, by notice under section 67 given ... within the period referred to in
-- paragraph (a), requests the claimant to give information ...--the end of the period of 12 days after the employer
-- receives the information ...; (c) if ... the Authority ... allows a further period ...--the end of that period". s 72
-- (death: 60 days) and s 73A (permanent impairment: 30 days): the period "is increased by the number of days occurring
-- after the day on which the request was made and before the day on which the employer receives the information"; and the
-- Authority may allow further periods. ss 72(5), 73(6), 73A(6): if not determined by then, "the employer is taken to have
-- made a decision, at the end of that period, disallowing the claim."
DECLARE `Claim for the time limit` IS ONE OF
    `incapacity for work, property, or the cost of medical treatment (s 73)`
    `compensation on a death (s 72)`
    `permanent impairment (s 73A)`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim for the time limit`
      `the day the employer received the claim` IS A DATE
      `the employer asked for information within the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE
      `the day it received the information` IS A DATE
      `the Authority allowed a further period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the end of the further period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the employer to determine the claim` MEANS
    IF `the Authority allowed a further period` AND `the end of the further period` GREATER THAN `the statutory deadline`
    THEN `the end of the further period`
    ELSE `the statutory deadline`
    WHERE
        `the days of the request` MEANS
            IF `the employer asked for information within the period`
            THEN max 0 (DATE_SERIAL `the day it received the information` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day it asked` MINUS 1)
            ELSE 0
        `the statutory deadline` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the claim`
            WHEN `incapacity for work, property, or the cost of medical treatment (s 73)`
                 THEN IF     `the employer asked for information within the period`
                         AND (`the day it received the information` PLUS 12) GREATER THAN (`the day the employer received the claim` PLUS 12)
                      THEN `the day it received the information` PLUS 12
                      ELSE `the day the employer received the claim` PLUS 12
            WHEN `compensation on a death (s 72)` THEN `the day the employer received the claim` PLUS (60 PLUS `the days of the request`)
            WHEN `permanent impairment (s 73A)` THEN `the day the employer received the claim` PLUS (30 PLUS `the days of the request`)

@export My employer has not decided my claim: after what day is it taken to have disallowed it (ss 72, 73, 73A)?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `Claim for the time limit` @desc What the claim is for
      `the day my employer received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received your claim
      `my employer asked me for information within the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, within the 12 days (incapacity, property, medical), 60 days (death) or 30 days (permanent impairment), your employer asked you by notice under s 67 for information, a document or an authority
      `the day it asked` IS A DATE @desc The day it asked (ignored if it did not)
      `the day it received what it asked for` IS A DATE @desc The day it received the information, document or authority (ignored if it did not ask)
      `the Authority allowed my employer a further period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Seafarers Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Authority allowed your employer a further period, by a notice served in time
      `the end of the further period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of that further period (ignored if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my employer decide my claim` MEANS
    `the last day for the employer to determine the claim` `the claim` `the day my employer received the claim` `my employer asked me for information within the period` `the day it asked` `the day it received what it asked for` `the Authority allowed my employer a further period` `the end of the further period`

§§ `s 28 -- travel to treatment`

-- s 28(6): the employer is liable for a necessary journey "from the place in Australia where the employee is residing to
-- the place where the treatment is to be obtained", and for staying there. (7): "not payable ... unless: (a) in relation to
-- a journey [by] public transport or ambulance services--the employee's injury reasonably required the use of public
-- transport or ambulance services ... regardless of the distance involved; or (b) in relation to a journey [by] private
-- motor vehicle--the reasonable length of such a journey exceeded 50 kilometres." The per-kilometre formula and rate are
-- not in the deposit.
@export Can I claim the cost of travelling to medical treatment for my injury (s 28(6), (7))?
GIVEN `the treatment is compensable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether compensation is payable for the medical treatment you travelled to
      `I went by public transport or ambulance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the journey was by public transport or ambulance (rather than private car)
      `my injury reasonably required it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For public transport or an ambulance: whether your injury reasonably required it
      `the reasonable length of the journey in kilometres` IS A NUMBER @desc For a private car: the reasonable length of the journey, including the return part, in kilometres
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I claim travel to treatment under the Seafarers Act` IF
        `the treatment is compensable`
    AND (    (`I went by public transport or ambulance` AND `my injury reasonably required it`)
         OR  ((NOT `I went by public transport or ambulance`) AND `the reasonable length of the journey in kilometres` GREATER THAN 50))

§§ `ss 31, 38 -- weekly compensation for incapacity` -- arises only if the person cannot work, or not at the same rank

-- s 31(2), (3): for "each of the first 45 weeks (whether consecutive or otherwise) during which the employee is
-- incapacitated" (for a seafarer, the first 45 weeks "after the date on which the seafarer is left on shore at, or
-- returned to, his or her home port"), an amount by a formula lost from the deposit. (4), (5): for every other week:
-- "(a) if the employee is not employed during that week--an amount equal to 75% of his or her normal weekly earnings less
-- the amount (if any) that he or she was able to earn during that week in suitable employment"; (b) to (f): an amount
-- that, with what the employee was able to earn in suitable employment, makes 80% (employed 25% or less of normal weekly
-- hours), 85% (over 25%, not over 50%), 90% (over 50%, not over 75%), 95% (over 75%, under 100%) or 100% (100%) of
-- normal weekly earnings. (6): if employed "as a seafarer" in the week, as if (f) applied. (7): reduced to 150% of AWOTE.
-- (8): an amount under (5)(a) below "the minimum earnings" is increased to them; (9): the minimum earnings are the lesser
-- of "$254.46" (plus "$62.99" for prescribed persons wholly or mainly dependent, (10), and "$31.50" for each prescribed
-- child, (11)) and "90% of the employee's normal weekly earnings"; these figures are indexed by s 23 (inputs).
-- s 38(1): not payable to an employee "who has reached pension age"; (2): if injured at or after "the age that is one year
-- before pension age", payable "for a maximum of 52 weeks"; (3): not while imprisoned for an offence.
GIVEN `the hours I was employed this week` IS A NUMBER
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
      `I worked as a seafarer this week` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 31(5) percentage` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I worked as a seafarer this week` THEN 100
        IF `the hours I was employed this week` AT MOST 0 THEN 75
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.25 THEN 80
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.5 THEN 85
        IF `the share` AT MOST 0.75 THEN 90
        IF `the share` LESS THAN 1 THEN 95
        OTHERWISE 100
    WHERE
        `the share` MEANS `the hours I was employed this week` DIVIDED BY `my normal weekly hours`

GIVEN `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `what I could earn this week in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours I was employed this week` IS A NUMBER
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
      `I worked as a seafarer this week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `AWOTE` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum earnings base` IS A NUMBER
      `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` IS A NUMBER
      `the addition for each prescribed child` IS A NUMBER
      `a prescribed person depends on me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed children who depend on me` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 31(5) amount` MEANS
    IF     `not employed (s 31(5)(a))`
       AND `the capped amount` LESS THAN `the minimum earnings`
    THEN `the minimum earnings`
    ELSE `the capped amount`
    WHERE
        `the percentage` MEANS `the s 31(5) percentage` `the hours I was employed this week` `my normal weekly hours` `I worked as a seafarer this week`
        `not employed (s 31(5)(a))` MEANS `the percentage` EQUALS 75
        `the amount` MEANS max 0 ((`my normal weekly earnings` TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100) MINUS `what I could earn this week in suitable employment`)
        `the capped amount` MEANS min `the amount` (1.5 TIMES `AWOTE`)
        `the dependants' additions` MEANS
            (IF `a prescribed person depends on me` THEN `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` ELSE 0)
            PLUS (`the prescribed children who depend on me` TIMES `the addition for each prescribed child`)
        `the minimum earnings` MEANS min (`the minimum earnings base` PLUS `the dependants' additions`) (0.9 TIMES `my normal weekly earnings`)

DECLARE `Weekly compensation` IS ONE OF
    `one of the first 45 weeks: compensation by the s 31(2) formula, which is not in the deposited text`
    `an amount per week after the first 45 weeks (s 31(4), (5))` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `none: I have reached pension age (s 38(1))`
    `none: the 52 weeks for an injury suffered within a year before pension age are used up (s 38(2))`
    `none: I am imprisoned for an offence (s 38(3))`
    `none: I am not incapacitated for work this week`

@export How much weekly compensation do I get for my incapacity this week (ss 31, 38)?
GIVEN `I am incapacitated for work this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of the injury, you cannot work at all this week, or cannot work at the same rank or level as before the injury
      `the weeks of incapacity before this one` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier weeks of incapacity count towards the first 45 (for a seafarer, weeks after you were left on shore at, or returned to, your home port)
      `my normal weekly earnings` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly earnings before the injury, in dollars (worked out under s 13)
      `what I could earn this week in suitable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What your employer determines you were able to earn this week in suitable employment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the hours I was employed this week` IS A NUMBER @desc The hours you were employed this week (0 if none)
      `my normal weekly hours` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly hours (ashore: those in your award, agreement or the NES, or 38)
      `I worked as a seafarer this week` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were employed or engaged as a seafarer for any part of this week
      `AWOTE` IS A NUMBER @desc The Australian Statistician's Average Weekly Ordinary Time Earnings of full-time adults, in dollars
      `the minimum earnings base` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(9)(a) minimum earnings figure in force, in dollars ($254.46 in this compilation, indexed each 1 July under s 23)
      `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(10) addition in force, in dollars ($62.99 in this compilation, indexed)
      `the addition for each prescribed child` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 31(11) addition per child in force, in dollars ($31.50 in this compilation, indexed)
      `a prescribed person depends on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse, or another prescribed person (an adult relative, or someone caring for your child), is wholly or mainly dependent on you
      `the prescribed children who depend on me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many prescribed children (children under 16, or students under 25) are wholly or mainly dependent on you, not counting a child already counted as the prescribed person
      `I have reached pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have reached pension age under the Social Security Act 1991
      `I was injured within a year before pension age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured at or after the age one year before your pension age
      `the weeks of incapacity already compensated` IS A NUMBER @desc How many weeks of incapacity have already been compensated for this injury (counted only for an injury within a year before pension age)
      `I am imprisoned for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in prison this week for committing an offence
GIVETH A `Weekly compensation`
`How much weekly compensation this week` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I am incapacitated for work this week`) THEN `none: I am not incapacitated for work this week`
        IF `I am imprisoned for an offence` THEN `none: I am imprisoned for an offence (s 38(3))`
        IF `I was injured within a year before pension age` AND `the weeks of incapacity already compensated` AT LEAST 52
            THEN `none: the 52 weeks for an injury suffered within a year before pension age are used up (s 38(2))`
        IF `I have reached pension age` AND (NOT `I was injured within a year before pension age`)
            THEN `none: I have reached pension age (s 38(1))`
        IF `the weeks of incapacity before this one` LESS THAN 45
            THEN `one of the first 45 weeks: compensation by the s 31(2) formula, which is not in the deposited text`
        OTHERWISE `an amount per week after the first 45 weeks (s 31(4), (5))` (`the s 31(5) amount` `my normal weekly earnings` `what I could earn this week in suitable employment` `the hours I was employed this week` `my normal weekly hours` `I worked as a seafarer this week` `AWOTE` `the minimum earnings base` `the addition for a dependent prescribed person` `the addition for each prescribed child` `a prescribed person depends on me` `the prescribed children who depend on me`)

§§ `ss 39, 40 -- permanent impairment` -- arises only if the injury has left a permanent impairment

-- s 39(3), (4): "the same percentage of the maximum amount as the percentage determined under subsection (5)" (the degree
-- under the approved Guide), "not more than the maximum amount at the date of the assessment". (7): nothing "where the
-- degree of permanent impairment ... is less than 10%"; (8): except the loss or loss of use of a finger or toe, or loss of
-- taste or smell. (9): "the maximum amount is $100,778.56", indexed under s 23 (an input). s 40(4): after a final
-- assessment, nothing for an increase "unless the increase is 10% or more". (No separate hearing-loss threshold, unlike
-- the SRC Act.)
@export How much permanent impairment compensation will I get under the Seafarers Act (s 39)?
GIVEN `it is the loss of a finger, toe, taste or smell` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the impairment is the loss, or loss of use, of a finger or toe, or the loss of the sense of taste or smell
      `the degree of permanent impairment` IS A NUMBER @desc The degree of permanent impairment your employer determines under the approved Guide, as a percentage
      `the maximum amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 39 maximum amount in force at the date of assessment, in dollars ($100,778.56 in this compilation, indexed each 1 July under s 23)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much permanent impairment compensation under the Seafarers Act` MEANS
    IF `the degree of permanent impairment` LESS THAN 10 AND (NOT `it is the loss of a finger, toe, taste or smell`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `the maximum amount` (`the maximum amount` TIMES `the degree of permanent impairment` DIVIDED BY 100)

§§ `s 29 -- if the employee dies` -- arises only if the injury results in death; asked by a dependant

-- s 29(2): "if the employee dies without leaving dependants, compensation is not payable for the injury" (apart from ss 28
-- and 30). (3): if some dependants were wholly dependent, "compensation of $412,000 is payable" for their benefit. (4): if
-- only partly dependent dependants, "such amount, not exceeding $412,000, as is appropriate, having regard to any losses
-- suffered by those dependants". (5): "$113.30 per week" for each prescribed child. s 23A indexes these (inputs).
DECLARE `Lump sum on death` IS ONE OF
    `the full lump sum, for all the dependants, shared as the employer determines (s 29(3), (8))` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `an appropriate amount, up to this, for the partly dependent dependants (s 29(4))` HAS `at most` IS A NUMBER
    `no lump sum: the employee left no dependants (s 29(2)); medical and funeral costs are still payable (ss 28, 30)`

@export A seafarer in my family died of a work injury: what lump sum is payable to the dependants (s 29(2) to (4))?
GIVEN `some dependants were wholly dependent on the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any dependant was wholly dependent on the employee for economic support at the date of death
      `some dependants were partly dependent on the employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any dependant was partly dependent on the employee at that date
      `the s 29 lump sum in force` IS A NUMBER @desc The s 29(3) amount in force, in dollars ($412,000 in this compilation, indexed each 1 July by the Wage Price Index under s 23A)
GIVETH A `Lump sum on death`
`What lump sum is payable on a seafarer's death` MEANS
    IF `some dependants were wholly dependent on the employee`
    THEN `the full lump sum, for all the dependants, shared as the employer determines (s 29(3), (8))` `the s 29 lump sum in force`
    ELSE IF `some dependants were partly dependent on the employee`
         THEN `an appropriate amount, up to this, for the partly dependent dependants (s 29(4))` `the s 29 lump sum in force`
         ELSE `no lump sum: the employee left no dependants (s 29(2)); medical and funeral costs are still payable (ss 28, 30)`

§§ `ss 78, 88 -- reconsideration and review`

-- s 78(2), (3): a claimant may ask the employer, in writing, to reconsider a determination, giving reasons, "within 30
-- days after the day on which the determination first came to the notice of the claimant, or within such further period
-- (if any) as the employer ... allows". (4), (5): the employer reconsiders with an industry panel or a Comcare officer.
-- s 76: "reviewable decision means a decision made under section 78"; s 88(1), (2): only the claimant may apply to the
-- ART, for review of a reviewable decision.
@export By what day must I ask my employer to reconsider its determination on my claim (s 78(3))?
GIVEN `the day the determination first came to my notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you first learned of your employer's determination
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask my employer to reconsider` MEANS `the day the determination first came to my notice` PLUS 30

DECLARE `Review` IS ONE OF
    `first ask my employer in writing to reconsider it, within 30 days (s 78); only the decision on reconsideration can go to the ART (ss 76, 88)`
    `I may apply to the ART for review of the reconsideration decision (s 88(1))`

@export Can I take my employer's decision on my claim to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ss 76, 78, 88)?
GIVEN `the determination has been reconsidered under s 78` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has reconsidered the determination under s 78 and made a decision affirming, varying or revoking it (or is taken to have disallowed it under s 79(6))
GIVETH A `Review`
`Can I go to the ART` MEANS
    IF `the determination has been reconsidered under s 78`
    THEN `I may apply to the ART for review of the reconsideration decision (s 88(1))`
    ELSE `first ask my employer in writing to reconsider it, within 30 days (s 78); only the decision on reconsideration can go to the ART (ss 76, 88)`
